assive fundraising edge: $42.6M cash vs Collins' $2.1M", "Expert consensus of Likely D across ten raters", "Prediction markets price Ossoff at 94-95%"], "rationale": "Polls uniformly show Ossoff ahead, with even Republican-leaning pollsters giving him 4-7 point leads, and he holds an overwhelming financial advantage. Ratings cluster at Likely D and markets price him near 95%, so a Likely D forecast with a mid-single-digit margin fits the evidence, tempered slightly by headlines suggesting tightening.", "watch": "A late shift in the national midterm environment or a polling consolidation behind Collins could narrow the race toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Georgia's Senate race pits incumbent Democrat Jon Ossoff against Republican Congressman Mike Collins. Ossoff has led in every public poll this cycle, with recent surveys from YouGov and several Republican-affiliated pollsters showing margins between four and ten points. He has also built a dominant financial position, raising over $77 million and holding $42.6 million on hand, while Collins has raised about $7.4 million and relies more heavily on outside groups.\n\nForecasters broadly rate the race Likely Democratic, with one rating it Tilt D and markets pricing Ossoff's chances around 94-95%. Some recent coverage notes the race tightening as Collins gains name recognition, but the polling and financial evidence still points clearly toward Ossoff, with the state's near-even partisan lean making a blowout unlikely.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}]}